fixer_verifier_output.raw_output:
Plan and patch summary for bmp color profile bounds checks

Root cause:
- The code path bmp_read_color_profile for ICC profiles (colorspacetype 0x4d424544) reads info->profileoffset and info->profilesize without fully validating that the profile fits within the provided BMP color data buffer. This can cause memcpy/copy to read past the end when end-begin is smaller than profile offset + profilesize, triggering AddressSanitizer crashes.

Minimal, focused fix (2-3 lines of logic, no API changes):
- In the 0x4d424544 branch, before creating the profile buffer, compute available as (size_t)(end - begin).
- If info->profileoffset >= available, warn and return NULL.
- Clamp info->profilesize to the remaining bytes: max_read = available - info->profileoffset; if (info->profilesize > max_read) info->profilesize = (uint32_t)max_read.
- If info->profilesize == 0, warn and return NULL.
- Then allocate profile from begin + info->profileoffset with the clamped info->profilesize.

Proposed patch (diff-like snippet):
--- a/src/mupdf/source/fitz/load-bmp.c
+++ b/src/mupdf/source/fitz/load-bmp.c
@@
-        {
-            fz_warn(ctx, "ignoring truncated color profile in bmp image");
-            return NULL;
-        }
-
-        profile = fz_new_buffer_from_copied_data(ctx, begin + info->profileoffset, info->profilesize);
+        /* Validate bounds for ICC color profile to avoid out-of-bounds reads */
+        size_t available = (size_t)(end - begin);
+        if (info->profileoffset >= available) {
+            fz_warn(ctx, "ignoring color profile with offset beyond buffer in bmp image");
+            return NULL;
+        }
+        {
+            size_t max_read = available - info->profileoffset;
+            if (info->profilesize > max_read)
+                info->profilesize = (uint32_t)max_read;
+            if (info->profilesize == 0) {
+                fz_warn(ctx, "ignoring empty color profile in bmp image");
+                return NULL;
+            }
+        }
+        profile = fz_new_buffer_from_copied_data(ctx, begin + info->profileoffset, info->profilesize);
*** End Patch

Rationale:
- This enforces the exact bounds of the input buffer and prevents reading beyond end, which caused the ASan crash observed in the crash report. The change is minimal, localized to the ICC color profile path and preserves existing semantics when the data is valid or partially truncated (it simply clamps to available bytes and warns when empty).

Verification steps (after patch):
- Build: secb build
- Run repro: secb repro and observe no ASAN read faults in bmp color profile path.

Notes:
- If there are multiple similar patterns for other color profile types, apply the same bound checks analogously, but only ICC (BMPRGB) requires this extra guard based on the crash description.

